      "content": "Those moments of questioning the point of anything are often the deepest signs of despair, and it sounds like the exhaustion is immense. Instead of focusing on the future or the 'point,' perhaps try focusing on the immediate, tiny sensation of the warmth from the tea. You don't have to belong; you just have to occupy this space for this single breath. Sometimes, the only task is to simply remain present with the next small moment.",
